  "registration_anchor_rules": [
    "anchor_kind is resolved through did-method-adapter-registry.json registration_anchor_kind before any branch parsing; an unregistered value, including any did:web anchor, fails closed with unsupported_did_method.",
    "webvh_registration derivation: log_entries MUST begin at inception (previous_entry_digest null) and chain by sha256 over RFC 8785 JCS of the preceding entry; registration_did_operation.did_method MUST equal webvh and its operation.version_id MUST equal the terminal entry version_id; every entry with witness_threshold > 0 MUST be covered by at least that many witness_records for its exact version_id, and a record for a version outside log_entries is surplus. did is registration_did_operation.did, version_id is the terminal entry version_id and method_history_head is sha256 over RFC 8785 JCS of the terminal entry.",
    "did_key_registration derivation: the branch carries only anchor_kind and did. method_history_head is sha256 over the UTF-8 bytes of did, version_id is synthetic-did-sha256:<same hex>, and the normalized document, root verification method and root key are rebuilt from the multibase suffix alone.",
    "The derived did, method_history_head and version_id MUST equal the PCR genesis initial_resolution values byte-for-byte, the derived root verification method and key MUST equal the genesis root producer material, and project(did) MUST equal account_id.principal_id.",
    "Every check consumes only the evidence root and its explicitly referenced objects. No case supplies a current resolver result, a database projection or an Account Authority receipt, so the whole suite runs offline."
  ],
